# ☁️ Cloud Storage Backup Automator

A Python tool that automates backing up local files and folders to AWS S3 cloud storage, with automatic bucket creation, date-organized backups, and backup listing.

Built to apply Cloud Computing concepts learned during my Big Data & Cloud Computing internship (YBI Foundation).

## 💡 Features
- Automatically creates an S3 bucket if it doesn't exist
- Uploads single files or entire folders (recursively)
- Organizes backups by date for easy tracking
- Lists all existing backups with file size and last-modified date
- Clear error handling for missing credentials or failed uploads

## 🛠️ Tech Used
- Python 3
- boto3 (AWS SDK for Python)

## 🚀 How to Run
1. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   pip install boto3
   ```
2. Configure AWS credentials:
   ```bash
   aws configure
   ```
3. Run the script:
   ```bash
   python cloud_backup.py
   ```
4. Enter your S3 bucket name and the local folder you want to back up.

## 📷 Example Output
```
=== Cloud Storage Backup Automator ===

Enter your S3 bucket name: my-backup-bucket
Enter the local folder path to back up: ./documents

Bucket 'my-backup-bucket' already exists.
Uploaded: ./documents/report.pdf -> s3://my-backup-bucket/backup/2026-08-11/report.pdf
Uploaded: ./documents/notes.txt -> s3://my-backup-bucket/backup/2026-08-11/notes.txt

Backup complete. Uploaded: 2, Failed: 0

--- Backups in 'my-backup-bucket' ---
backup/2026-08-11/report.pdf  (245.3 KB)  Last modified: 2026-08-11 10:20:00+00:00
backup/2026-08-11/notes.txt  (2.1 KB)  Last modified: 2026-08-11 10:20:01+00:00
```

